  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1254 PM CDT Tue Jul 14 2026\n\nOnce we get through tomorrow morning, most but not all the models\nhave the rainfall tapering off during the day and then\nredeveloping again tomorrow night into Thursday morning. Again,\nwhere the MCV ends up will be the biggest question, but the\nmajority of the models eventually drift the MCV a little to the\nwest and northwest. Of concern is that some of the models like \nthe NAM show a much stronger low level jet developing (40+ kts) \nacross the Northern Edwards Plateau and western Concho Valley \ntomorrow night. If this does develop and if the MCV is there \n(both big if's this far in advance), then the potential for heavy \nrainfall spreading north into the Concho Valley and perhaps San \nAngelo.\n\nHave coordinated with WPC and the excessive rainfall folks and \nwill see a northward expansion of the High and Moderate ERO's \ninto West Central Texas for Day 2 and Day 3. \n\nHeavy rainfall threat may well linger into Friday but there are so\nmuch uncertainty about where the best potential will be that will\nnot go into much detail. MCV does eventually dissipate and the\nlatest model blends are ending precip for the weekend into early \nnext week. Should see temperatures begin to climb as well.",
